        "caption": {
          "zh": "1884–86年 · 芝加哥艺术博物馆",
          "en": "1884–86 · Art Institute of Chicago"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT I",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第一幕 · 河对岸的岛",
          "en": "The island across the river"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "1884年，修拉画完了《阿涅尔的浴场》。画面右边那座小岛，就是大碗岛。同一年，他开始画这幅更大的画。",
          "en": "In 1884, Seurat finished *Bathers at Asnières*. The island on its right is La Grande Jatte. That same year, he began this even larger painting."
        }
      },
      {
        "image": "images/grande-jatte.jpg",
        "alt": {
          "zh": "修拉《大碗岛的星期天下午》1884–86，芝加哥艺术博物馆",
          "en": "Georges Seurat, A Sunday on La Grande Jatte — 1884, 1884–86, Art Institute of Chicago"
        },
        "caption": {
          "zh": "1884–86年 · 芝加哥艺术博物馆",
          "en": "1884–86 · Art Institute of Chicago"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT II",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第二幕 · 一个点一个点",
          "en": "Dot by dot"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "他用了两年时间，先画横向的笔触，再一个点一个点地画。他说，他想用希腊古典浮雕的方式，表现现代生活。",
          "en": "He worked on it for two years, first with horizontal strokes, then dot by dot. He said he wanted to represent modern life in the manner of a classical Greek frieze."
        }
      },
      {
        "image": "images/grande-jatte.jpg",
        "alt": {
          "zh": "修拉《大碗岛的星期天下午》1884–86，芝加哥艺术博物馆",
          "en": "Georges Seurat, A Sunday on La Grande Jatte — 1884, 1884–86, Art Institute of Chicago"
        },
        "caption": {
          "zh": "1884–86年 · 芝加哥艺术博物馆",
          "en": "1884–86 · Art Institute of Chicago"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT III",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第三幕 · 最后一届印象派画展",
          "en": "The last Impressionist exhibition"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "1886年5月，这幅画在第八届、也是最后一届印象派画展上首次展出。1926年起，它成为芝加哥艺术博物馆的永久收藏。",
          "en": "In May 1886, the painting was first shown at the eighth and last Impressionist exhibition. Since 1926 it has been in the permanent collection of the Art Institute of Chicago."
        }
      }
